< < \tfrac12\) and \(F(1) = \tfrac34 \ge \tfrac12\). The least value whose distribution function reaches \(\tfrac12\) is 1 (Lesson 1, Proposition 3.2). The same convention as rung 1 applies: the quantile is the least value whose distribution function reaches the level (Lesson 1, Proposition 3.2). Rung 1 takes the rank \(\lceil 0.99\, n \rceil\) of its sorted losses (project.html, Rungs 1 and 2). Proposition 3.4 states that rank for distinct values, and the whole-cent losses of rung 1 can repeat.</p>
